lue of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years. In 2025, November to December ran 63% of normal on the middle of the grids, while September to October ran 128%. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 19985 at 67% of normal that year. The preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 on grid 19686 sits at 78.2.</p>"}
